# Build context was 1.24GB without this file (measured: .venv 943M, data 282M,
# warehouse 10M, web 6.2M) -- every `make image` shipped all of it to the
# daemon even though the Dockerfile only COPYs src/, scripts/, config.yml,
# requirements.txt. Also a correctness guard: without this, a `COPY .`-style
# change to the Dockerfile would bake a macOS/arm .venv and a laptop-lineage
# Iceberg warehouse (absolute paths baked into its metadata.json -- see
# docs/spark-notes.md "Never copy a Hadoop-catalog Iceberg warehouse") into
# the image.
.venv/
data/
warehouse/
warehouse-k8s/
web/
notebooks/
.git/
__pycache__/
docs/img/
